# Cancel/replace desk
#
# Shows:   reacting to cancel and replace requests while an order works:
#          `when` handlers, first match wins, `history`, the too-late reject
# Needs:   any session that receives orders
# Watch:   Received Orders: Pending, Pending ID, New Qty, New Px
# Outcome: the first replace is accepted, later ones refused; a cancel is
#          accepted unless the order has finished

on order where symbol != ''
    after 100ms
    accept

    # A `when` is live from this line to the end of its block, and runs beside
    # the lines below it. For one event the first `when` that matches wins, so
    # the special cases come first.

    # `history` is every recorded version of the order's row; event.request is
    # the ClOrdID of the request in hand. A version that held some other
    # replace request means this one is not the first.
    when replace and ANY(history, h -> h.pending_action == 'Replace' and h.pending_cl_ord_id != event.request)
        reject text: 'one replace per order'

    # A replace below what has already traded cannot be honoured.
    when replace and order.pending_qty < order.cum_qty
        reject text: 'below executed quantity'

    when replace
        after 250ms ± 50ms
        accept

    # Too late: the order finished before the cancel arrived.
    when cancel and order.leaves_qty == 0
        reject text: 'too late to cancel'

    when cancel
        after 500ms
        accept
        stop

    # Meanwhile the order keeps filling. A request stays parked while fills
    # continue, exactly as on Received Orders by hand.
    while order.leaves_qty > 0
        after 2s
        fill qty: MIN(100, order.leaves_qty), price: order.price
